diff --git a/docs/1.guide/1.basics/6.error.md b/docs/1.guide/1.basics/6.error.md
index 8bc22d4..1efcf48 100644
--- a/docs/1.guide/1.basics/6.error.md
+++ b/docs/1.guide/1.basics/6.error.md
@@ -75,6 +75,44 @@ This will end the request with `400 - Bad Request` status code and the following
 > [!IMPORTANT]
 > Error `statusText` should be short (max 512 to 1024 characters) and only include tab, spaces or visible ASCII characters and extended characters (byte value 128–255). Prefer `message` in JSON body for extended message.
 
+## Problem Details (RFC 9457)
+
+Use `problem()` to send an error as [`application/problem+json`](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457). It takes the same fields as `HTTPError` plus the optional `type` and `instance` members, and returns an `HTTPError`:
+
+```js
+import { problem, getRouterParam } from "h3";
+
+app.get("/users/:id", (event) => {
+  throw problem({
+    status: 404,
+    message: "User not found",
+    type: "https://example.com/errors/user-not-found",
+    instance: `/users/${getRouterParam(event, "id")}`,
+  });
+});
+```
+
+The response is:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "https://example.com/errors/user-not-found",
+  "title": "Not Found",
+  "status": 404,
+  "detail": "User not found",
+  "instance": "/users/7"
+}
+```
+
+- `type` defaults to `about:blank` and `instance` is only included when set.
+- `title` is `statusText` or, when missing, the standard phrase of the status. Statuses without a registered phrase use `HTTPError`.
+- `detail` is the `message`.
+- `body` properties are added at the top level and `data` under the `data` key. Reserved members (`type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`) cannot be overwritten by them.
+- With `unhandled: true`, `detail` is `HTTPError` and `data`, `body` and `instance` are omitted, as for other unhandled errors.
+- `headers` are applied, but `Content-Type` is always `application/problem+json`.
+
+Only errors created with `problem()` use this format. `new HTTPError(...)`, `HTTPError.status(...)` and errors passed as `cause` keep the default JSON format. `type` is not validated as a URI. JSON-RPC handlers do not use this format.
+
 ## Unhandled Errors
 
 Any error that occurs during calling [request lifecycle](/guide/basics/lifecycle) without using `HTTPError` will be processed as an _unhandled_ error.
